verl LoRA in-memory sync vs. the ScalarLM vLLM fork (farbodatdocker/scalarlm:mi355-v1.6)
========================================================================================
Functionally equivalent to the verl stack's own patch,
stacks/verl/verl_scalarlm_vllm_fork_lora.patch, re-derived for this tree.

Why: verl syncs the LoRA adapter trainer -> vLLM in memory by monkey-patching
`LRUCacheWorkerLoRAManager._load_adapter` to accept a `TensorLoRARequest`
(`VLLMHijack.hijack()` in verl/utils/vllm/utils.py). The ScalarLM fork replaces the worker
LoRA manager with `vllm/tokenformer/hybrid_adapter_manager.py::PTWorkerLoRAManager` (and
`HybridAdapterManager` when tokenformer is enabled too). Both override the entry points and
call `get_adapter_absolute_path(lora_request.lora_path)` / `load_adapter_from_pt()` on disk
*before* verl's patched method is reached, so the sync dies with
`OfflineModeIsEnabled ... snapshot_download("simon_lora_path")`.

Fix: route `TensorLoRARequest`s straight to verl's tensor loader on those two classes; any
other request keeps the fork's behaviour. Guarded by try/except ImportError so it is a no-op
on upstream vLLM. Applied with: cd /opt/verl && patch -p1 < this_file

--- a/verl/utils/vllm/utils.py
+++ b/verl/utils/vllm/utils.py
@@ -123,6 +123,38 @@ class VLLMHijack:
 
         do_hijack(LRUCacheWorkerLoRAManager, "_load_adapter", hijack__load_adapter)
 
+        # --- ScalarLM vLLM fork (farbodatdocker/scalarlm:mi355-v1.6) ---------------------
+        # The fork replaces the worker LoRA manager with PTWorkerLoRAManager (and wraps it
+        # in HybridAdapterManager when tokenformer is enabled). Both open lora_path on disk
+        # before the hijacked LRUCacheWorkerLoRAManager._load_adapter runs, which breaks
+        # verl's in-memory TensorLoRARequest sync. Route tensor requests straight to the
+        # loader above; leave every other request on the fork's own path.
+        try:
+            from vllm.tokenformer.hybrid_adapter_manager import HybridAdapterManager, PTWorkerLoRAManager
+        except ImportError:
+            return
+
+        _fork_pt_load_adapter = PTWorkerLoRAManager._load_adapter
+
+        def hijack_pt__load_adapter(self, lora_request):
+            if isinstance(lora_request, TensorLoRARequest):
+                return hijack__load_adapter(self, lora_request)
+            return _fork_pt_load_adapter(self, lora_request)
+
+        do_hijack(PTWorkerLoRAManager, "_load_adapter", hijack_pt__load_adapter)
+
+        _fork_hybrid_add_adapter = HybridAdapterManager.add_adapter
+
+        def hijack_hybrid_add_adapter(self, lora_request):
+            if isinstance(lora_request, TensorLoRARequest):
+                if self._lora is None:
+                    raise RuntimeError("TensorLoRARequest needs a LoRA-enabled HybridAdapterManager")
+                self._kinds[lora_request.adapter_id] = "lora"
+                return self._lora.add_adapter(lora_request)
+            return _fork_hybrid_add_adapter(self, lora_request)
+
+        do_hijack(HybridAdapterManager, "add_adapter", hijack_hybrid_add_adapter)
+
 
 def is_version_ge(pkg: str = "vllm", minver: str = "0.7.3"):
     """check if the package version is greater than or equal to the minimum version"""
